    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="60">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 60</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">{CIIII} Se ceorl se ðe hæfð oðres geoht ahyrod, gif he hæbbe ealle on forðre to agifanne, gesceawege mon, agife ealle. Gif he næbbe, agife healf on fodre, healfe on oþrum ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">A ceorl who has hired another’s yoke, if he is able to pay it all in fodder, make sure he gives all. If he cannot, let him pay half in fodder and half in other goods.</ab>
        <ab type="secondTranslation" xml:lang="en">If a commoner, who has hired another's yoke of oxen, is able to pay all the hire in fodder, care should be taken that he does pay it all [in this form]. If he is not able to do so, he shall pay half [the hire] in fodder, and half in other goods.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Se ciorl þe hæbbe oðres geoht ahyred, gif he hæbbe ealle on forðre to agyfanne, gesceawege mon; gif he næbbe, agife healf on foðre, healf on oþrum ceape.</ab>
      </div>
